 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Learn the basics in the present tense, and the past too. Walk, run, jump, I always trip. Pretty close. Walk, run, jump, I always trip. Walk, run, jump, I tripped last week. Also learn the gender endings for people, for example, man ends in an i, woman ends in an a. It takes little while, but it sticks. Meanwhile you can use the personal pronouns she, he, it, they, and I. Lots of learners do. I is the self pronoun, not me. You do. Learn the basic colors, then add shades, tints, and mixes.",
